    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Babur introduced the Tulghuma warfare strategy and gunpowder artillery for the first time in Northern India at the First Battle of Panipat (1526).",
        "The Treaty of Allahabad (1765) signed after the Battle of Buxar granted Diwani rights (tax collection) to the British East India Company.",
        "Competitive exams frequently test the chronological order of the three Battles of Panipat: 1526 (Babur vs. Lodi), 1556 (Akbar vs. Hemu), and 1761 (Marathas vs. Ahmad Shah Abdali)."
      ],
      "id": "z6oi6sh"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Battle of Hydaspes (326 BC) was fought between Alexander the Great and King Porus along the banks of the Jhelum River.",
        "The First Battle of Panipat (1526) led to the establishment of Mughal rule in India by Babur against Ibrahim Lodi.",
        "The Battle of Plassey (1757) marked the beginning of British political control in India after Siraj-ud-Daulah was defeated due to betrayal by Mir Jafar.",
        "The Battle of Buxar (1764) resulted in the Treaty of Allahabad (1765), granting Diwani rights of Bengal, Bihar, and Orissa to the East India Company."
      ],
      "id": "np8fbzs"
    }
